  "pseudos": [
    {
      "id": "p1",
      "text": "After the medical entrance exam on May 3, 2026, an alert explorer sent the National Testing Agency a PDF file that matched the chemistry paper exactly, charting a new path of digital evidence. This frontier discovery prompted the NTA to hand over 26-27 test developers and translators to the Central Bureau of Investigation, initiating a boundary-transfer action. Subsequent investigations led to the arrest of thirteen individuals, including a trainer, effectively tracking and constraining those who had crossed the line, while the cancelled NEET-UG exam opened a reset opportunity for the system.",
      "source": {
        "agent_id": "The-Explorer",
        "fragments": [
          "why-0",
          "how-1",
          "how-2",
          "how-3",
          "result-0"
        ]
      },
      "warnings": [],
      "fit": 0.85
    },
    {
      "id": "p2",
      "text": "The NTA, acting as a boundary guardian, moved swiftly after receiving the tip-off. By June 21, 2026, a new journey begins for candidates with the rescheduled exam, following the system's disruption. The investigation, led by the CBI, resulted in thirteen rule-breakers being arrested, a clear constraint on those who trespassed. The entire episode, from the initial report to the arrests, underscores a broader reset in how educational frontiers are policed and explored.",
      "source": {
        "agent_id": "The-Explorer",
        "fragments": [
          "how-1",
          "how-2",
          "how-3",
          "how-4",
          "result-2",
